# Active Directory DNS Integration Verification

## Business Scenario

> Active Directory environments rely heavily on DNS for authentication, domain controller discovery, and service communication. Domain Controllers use DNS records to locate services such as LDAP, Kerberos, and other Active Directory components. Incorrect DNS configuration can result in domain join failures, authentication problems, slow logins, and Group Policy issues. Validating DNS functionality is an essential step after deploying Active Directory infrastructure.

---

## Project Objective

> Verify and document the DNS components required to support Active Directory Domain Services. The goal is to confirm that LABDC01 is providing DNS functionality, that Active Directory-integrated DNS zones exist, and that DNS services are prepared to support domain authentication and service discovery.

