## Best Practices

* Domain Controllers should use internal DNS servers for Active Directory communication.
* Avoid configuring domain systems to rely on public DNS providers.
* Validate DNS after Domain Controller deployment.
* Monitor DNS health using tools such as `dcdiag`.
* Document DNS zones and records.
* Confirm DNS functionality before troubleshooting higher-level Active Directory issues.

